# asdf's pin for this repository. It MUST name the same version as the
# `channel` in rust-toolchain.toml, which is rustup's pin for the same thing:
# two tools read two different files, and a contributor using the other one
# would otherwise silently build with a different compiler than CI.
# See "Bumping Rust" in CONTRIBUTING.md - both lines move in that one commit.
#
# Why pin at all: the lint levels in Cargo.toml's [workspace.lints] are `deny`,
# so a newer Clippy can fail a build nobody touched. Why pin here as well as in
# rust-toolchain.toml: asdf does not read rust-toolchain.toml, and a distro
# `cargo` (Arch's `rust` package, for instance) reads neither.
#
#   asdf plugin add rust https://github.com/asdf-community/asdf-rust.git
#   asdf install
#
# Note the asdf rust plugin installs a standalone toolchain, not rustup, so
# `rustup target add ...` is not available under it; the wasm32 target and the
# macOS cross targets need rustup (see CONTRIBUTING.md's Prerequisites).
rust 1.98.1
